    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "DAY6 — You Were Beautiful",
      "content": "Describing changes of state. \"It's getting colder.\" \"I'm becoming lonely.\"\n\nOne of DAY6's signature songs, built almost entirely around a single repeated word: 예뻤어 — 'you were beautiful,' past tense. The singer is clear upfront that he's not trying to get back together — he's just been hit by a memory and wants to say it out loud once.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-아/어지다**, which means \"to become a state.\" We'll see how DAY6 uses it in \"You Were Beautiful.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **멀어지다** — to grow distant\n- **슬프다** — to be sad\n- **멀어지고 있다** — to be growing distant\n- **슬퍼지다** — to become sad\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
